*==============================================================================
* FDOPAMP_FULL - behavioural fully differential op-amp macromodel (PSpice port)
*
* Copyright (c) 2026 Stanislav Maslovski
* SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause  (see LICENSE)
* Version 1.5.1 (2026-11). Developed with the help of Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic).
* PSpice port, generated by tools/make_pspice_port.py from ../fdopamp_full.lib.
* Do not edit by hand: change the main library and run the script again.
* Same pins, parameters and behaviour as the main library (checked against
* ngspice with tests/cross_sim.py). Tested with PSpice 9.1 (1999 evaluation
* version), so it should also run in later PSpice releases. Differences:
*   - B sources and parameter-gain E/G/H sources are E/G VALUE={} sources;
*     ?: is IF().
*   - The shared nodes of the main library (nvc, nsq, ncx, njhp, njhn, njlp,
*     njln, nim) are written out inside the expressions that use them, to stay
*     within the 64 nodes of the PSpice evaluation version (slower).
*   - VCMN defaults to 1e30, which means mid-supply (PSpice 9 cannot default a
*     parameter to an expression of other parameters).
*   - PSpice differentiates VALUE expressions numerically. To keep the small-
*     signal results exact, the output-stage command current is carried in mA
*     (nicmd...), the crossover input in mV (nvx...), and the clamp excesses on
*     their own nodes (nex...). 1e15 ohm partners give the 1k noise references
*     the two connections PSpice requires.
*
* Pins: inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm
*   outp is the non-inverted output (in phase with inp), outn the inverted one.
*   vocm sets the output common-mode voltage. Left open, it floats to
*   mid-supply through an internal divider (2*RVOCM to each rail).
*
* DIFFERENTIAL-MODE (DM) PATH  (same structure as OPAMP_FULL)
*   - DC gain A0, dominant pole, GBW, two extra poles (FP2, FP3)
*   - input stage tanh() -> differential output slew rate SR
*   - optional follower jump from the input-pair tail capacitance (KJUMP)
*   - optional phase reversal through an input junction (PRHI, PRLO, VPRHI,
*     VPRLO, IPR): one-sided, with the input current and the source-resistance
*     dependence of real parts
*   - optional rail-to-rail input crossover: offset and bias-current step
*     (VCMT, VKT, DVOST, DIBT)
*   - input CM range window, input R/C, optional differential clamp
*     (anti-parallel diodes between inp and inn; no clamps to the rails)
*   - VOS, IB/IOS, CMRR(f), PSRR(f), white + 1/f voltage noise, white + 1/f
*     current noise (FCIN = 1/f corner, independent on each input; 0 = off)
* COMMON-MODE (CM) LOOP  (internal CMFB)
*   - senses the output CM (V(outp)+V(outn))/2 and compares it with V(vocm)
*   - CM error amplifier: DC gain A0CM, unity-gain frequency GBWCM, second
*     pole FPCM2, output CM slew rate SRCM, CM offset VOSCM
*   - CMRR, PSRR and the DM gain do not affect it (ideal CM/DM separation)
*   - optional output balance error: Vout,cm = V(vocm) + VOSCM + KBAL*Vod
* OUTPUT STAGES (one per output, as in OPAMP_FULL)
*   - V(outp) = Vcm + Vd/2, V(outn) = Vcm - Vd/2 behind ROUT each
*   - swing limits VHD/VLD, current limits ISRC/ISNK, crossover VXO, COUT
*   - supply current = quiescent + load currents from the right rail
*
* Defaults approximate a generic +/-5 V, 100 MHz bipolar FDA.
* Units: SR, SRCM in V/s. CMRR/PSRR as ratios (31.6k = 90 dB).
*
* Notes
*   - SR is the DIFFERENTIAL output slew rate (each output slews at SR/2).
*   - The DM node n1 holds the differential output voltage. It is clamped to
*     +/-2*min(V(vcc)-VHD-Vocm, Vocm-V(vee)-VLD), so the outputs saturate
*     symmetrically and recover quickly.
*   - FDOPAMP_CORE exposes the single-ended CM control path through the pins
*     cmo (CM amplifier output) and cmi (output-stage CM input), so that the
*     CM loop can be opened for loop-gain tests. FDOPAMP_FULL joins them.
*   - Portability: tested in ngspice-42 and LTspice 26, and the PSpice port
*     in PSpice 9.1 (tests/cross_sim.py; DC/AC/transient/noise agree). White
*     e_n is passed through the E source Ewn (LTspice ignores the noise of a
*     resistor that is read only inside a B-source expression). Nodes that
*     otherwise see only G elements and capacitors get a 1e15 ohm DC path to
*     ground (R*lk), which satisfies the floating-node checks of LTspice and
*     PSpice; their effect on gain and noise is negligible.
*     This file is the PSpice port.
*
* PARAMETERS  (name, unit, default, meaning)
*  Gain and frequency response
*   A0      V/V    100k     open-loop DC gain
*   GBW     Hz     100Meg   gain-bandwidth product (unity-gain frequency of the
*                           dominant-pole response)
*   FP2     Hz     0        second pole; 0 = 3*GBW (300Meg at the
*                           default GBW)
*   FP3     Hz     0        third pole; 0 = 10*GBW (1G)
*   SR      V/s    200Meg   slew rate of the DIFFERENTIAL output
*                           (each output slews at SR/2)
*   KJUMP   -      0        input-pair tail capacitance: output jump / fast
*                           input common-mode step (large-signal follower
*                           response); 0 = off. The sign gives the input-pair
*                           polarity: > 0 npn/nmos (jump on rising edges),
*                           < 0 pnp/pmos/p-JFET (jump on falling edges).
*                           uA741 (datasheet pulse response): KJUMP ~0.27
*                           with the default SR
*  Input DC errors and impedance
*   VOS     V      1m       input offset voltage, in series with the + input
*   IB      A      2u       input bias current (average of the two pins);
*                           IB > 0 flows into the pins (NPN), IB < 0 out (PNP)
*   IOS     A      0.1u     input offset current, I(inp) - I(inn)
*   RID     ohm    1Meg     differential input resistance (noiseless); its
*                           current saturates at |IB|, as in a bipolar pair
*   CID     F      1p       differential input capacitance
*   RIC     ohm    200Meg   common-mode input resistance of each input pin to
*                           ground (noiseless)
*   CIC     F      1p       common-mode input capacitance of each input pin to
*                           ground
*  Differential input clamp (two anti-parallel diodes between inp and inn;
*  there are no clamp diodes from the inputs to the supply rails)
*   VCLMP   V      100      forward voltage of each diode at 1 mA (set through
*                           the emission coefficient); 100 = no clamp.
*                           OP27-style clamp: VCLMP=0.7 RCLMP=100
*   RCLMP   ohm    100      series resistance of each clamp diode
*  Common-mode and supply rejection
*   CMRR    ratio  31.6k    DC CMRR (31.6k = 90 dB)
*   FCMRR   Hz     0        CMRR falls at 20 dB/dec above this frequency;
*                           0 = 31.6*GBW/CMRR, so that the CMRR is 30 dB
*                           at GBW (100k at the defaults)
*                           Keep CMRR*FCMRR/GBW >= 3 (10 dB at GBW): the
*                           CMRR error is in series with the input, and
*                           below that a follower's step response rings
*   PSRRP   ratio  10k      DC rejection of the positive supply
*   PSRRN   ratio  10k      DC rejection of the negative supply
*   FPSRR   Hz     0        PSRR falls at 20 dB/dec above this frequency;
*                           0 = 1e-3*GBW (100k at the default GBW)
*   FPSRRP  Hz     0        PSRR+ corner (positive supply); 0 = FPSRR
*   FPSRRN  Hz     0        PSRR- corner (negative supply); 0 = FPSRR
*   VCCN    V      5        nominal positive supply (PSRR reference)
*   VEEN    V      -5       nominal negative supply (PSRR reference)
*   VCMN    V      mid      input CM voltage at which VOS is specified; the
*                           CMRR error is (Vcm - VCMN)/CMRR
*  Noise
*   ENOISE  V/rtHz 5n       white input voltage noise density
*   FCEN    Hz     1k       1/f corner of the voltage noise
*   INOISE  A/rtHz 1p       white input current noise density, each input
*   FCIN    Hz     0        1/f corner of the current noise (independent on
*                           the two inputs); 0 = white only
*  Supplies, input range and output swing
*   ICCQ    A      10m      quiescent supply current, vcc to vee
*   ICMHI   V      1.5      input CM range: distance below vcc at which the
*                           input-stage gm has fallen to half (< 0: beyond rail)
*   ICMLO   V      1        the same, above vee
*   VK      V      0.1      width of the gm roll-off at the input-range edges
*   PRHI    -      0        phase reversal at the top: a junction of the input
*                           pair (npn base-collector) conducts near vcc; its
*                           current reverses the output, which runs to the
*                           wrong rail at about PRHI*SR; 0 = no junction.
*                           Typical 1..4
*   PRLO    -      0        the same at the bottom (p-JFET gate-drain)
*   VPRHI   V      0        position of the top junction: input voltage below
*                           vcc where the output flips (< 0: above vcc)
*   VPRLO   V      0        the same above vee
*   IPR     A      0        input current of a conducting junction (into the
*                           pin at the top, out of it at the bottom); about the
*                           tail current of the input pair. 0 = SR*1pF.
*                           A source resistance RS prevents the reversal while
*                           0.9*RS*IPR is larger than the overdrive
*   VCMT    V      1        rail-to-rail input crossover: position of the
*                           transition between the input pairs, below vcc
*   VKT     V      0.1      width of the crossover transition
*   DVOST   V      0        offset change across the transition (VOS applies
*                           below it); 0 = none
*   DIBT    A      0        bias-current change across the transition, each pin
*   VHD     V      1.2      minimum headroom, output to vcc (swing limit)
*   VLD     V      1.2      minimum headroom, output to vee (swing limit)
*  Output stage (per output)
*   ROUT    ohm    10       output resistance
*   COUT    F      1p       output capacitance to ground
*   ISRC    A      50m      maximum source current
*   ISNK    A      50m      maximum sink current
*   VXO     V      0        class-AB crossover dead zone: for |Iout| below about
*                           VXO/ROUT the small-signal output resistance is
*                           2*ROUT; 0 disables it
*  Common-mode loop and vocm pin (FDA only)
*   A0CM    V/V    10k      DC gain of the CM error amplifier
*   GBWCM   Hz     50Meg    unity-gain frequency of the CM error amplifier
*   FPCM2   Hz     0        second pole of the CM loop; 0 = 4*GBWCM
*                           (200Meg at the default GBWCM)
*   SRCM    V/s    100Meg   slew rate of the output CM voltage
*   VOSCM   V      1m       output CM offset: Vout,cm = V(vocm) + VOSCM
*   KBAL    -      0        output balance error: the output CM moves by KBAL
*                           times the differential output (datasheet dB -> ratio)
*   RVOCM   ohm    50k      vocm pin bias: 2*RVOCM (noiseless) to each rail,
*                           i.e. RVOCM to mid-supply when the pin is open
*   CVOCM   F      1p       vocm pin capacitance to ground
*==============================================================================

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* FDZCPL : out = K * (1 + s/(2*pi*FZ)) * in   (same as ZCPL in opamp_full.lib)
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt FDZCPL in out PARAMS: K=1u FZ=1k FHI=2G
.param TAUZ={1/(6.283185307*FZ)} CD=1n
Ek na 0 VALUE={(K)*V(in)}
Cd  in nx {CD}
Gd nx nv VALUE={(6.283185307*FHI*CD)*V(nx,nv)}
Vs  nv 0 0
Rlk nx 0 1e15
Ed out na VALUE={(K*TAUZ/CD)*I(Vs)}
.ends FDZCPL

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt FDOPAMP_CORE inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm cmo cmi
+ PARAMS:
+ A0=100k GBW=100Meg SR=200Meg FP2=0 FP3=0
+ VOS=1m IB=2u IOS=0.1u
+ RID=1Meg CID=1p RIC=200Meg CIC=1p
+ CMRR=31.6k FCMRR=0 PSRRP=10k PSRRN=10k FPSRR=0 FPSRRP=0 FPSRRN=0 VCCN=5 VEEN=-5
+ VCMN=1e30
+ ENOISE=5n FCEN=1k INOISE=1p FCIN=0
+ ICCQ=10m VHD=1.2 VLD=1.2 ICMHI=1.5 ICMLO=1 VK=0.1
+ ROUT=10 ISRC=50m ISNK=50m VXO=0 COUT=1p
+ VCLMP=100 RCLMP=100 KJUMP=0
+ PRHI=0 PRLO=0 VPRHI=0 VPRLO=0 IPR=0 VCMT=1 VKT=0.1 DVOST=0 DIBT=0 KBAL=0
+ A0CM=10k GBWCM=50Meg FPCM2=0 SRCM=100Meg VOSCM=1m
+ RVOCM=50k CVOCM=1p

* ---- derived constants -------------------------------------------------------
.param PI2=6.283185307
.param VCMX={IF(VCMN>1e29, 0.5*(VCCN+VEEN), VCMN)}   ; VCMN=1e30: mid-supply
.param C1V=1p
.param IMAXV={SR*C1V}
.param GM0={PI2*GBW*C1V}
.param R1V={A0/GM0}
.param ICMV={SRCM*C1V}
.param GMC={PI2*GBWCM*C1V}
.param RCV={A0CM/GMC}
.param VNTH={sqrt(4*1.380649e-23*300.15*1e3)}
.param IFL=10m
.param VTN={1.380649e-23*300.15/1.602176634e-19}
.param KFV={ENOISE*ENOISE*FCEN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param ESH2={4*1.602176634e-19*VTN*VTN/IFL}
.param GENV={sqrt(max(ENOISE*ENOISE-ESH2,0))/VNTH}
.param GNI={INOISE/VNTH}
* 1/f current noise (FCIN > 0): one more flicker diode pair per input, so the
* two pins get independent noise. The flicker voltage of the pair is scaled to
* VNI*sqrt(FCIN/f) with VNI = 1 uV/rtHz and converted to current by GFI =
* INOISE/VNI, giving INOISE^2*FCIN/f. The pair's shot noise then adds only
* (0.21n/1u)^2 = 4e-8 of INOISE^2. FCIN = 0 disables the sources (GFI = 0).
.param KFI={1e-12*FCIN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param GFI={IF(FCIN>0, INOISE/1u, 0)}

* ---- input network (noiseless; RID behind the series error voltage) ----------
* The current through RID saturates at |IB| (IB = 0: no limit), as the base
* currents of a bipolar pair do once one transistor takes the whole tail
* current; small-signal it is V(vd)/RID.
.param IDL={IF(abs(IB)>0, abs(IB), 1)}
.param KID={1/(RID*IDL)}
Gid inp inn VALUE={IDL*tanh(V(vd)*KID)}
Cid  inp inn {CID}
Gic1 inp 0 VALUE={(1/RIC)*V(inp)}
Gic2 inn 0 VALUE={(1/RIC)*V(inn)}
Cic1 inp 0 {CIC}
Cic2 inn 0 {CIC}
Ibp  inp 0 DC {IB+IOS/2}
Ibn  inn 0 DC {IB-IOS/2}
* shared nodes, each computed once per iteration (fewer, smaller expressions:
* every controlling node of a behavioural source costs a derivative tree)
Gibt1 inp 0 VALUE={DIBT*(0.5*(1+tanh(((0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))-V(vcc)+VCMT)/VKT)))}
Gibt2 inn 0 VALUE={DIBT*(0.5*(1+tanh(((0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))-V(vcc)+VCMT)/VKT)))}
Dp1  inp inn DIN
Dp2  inn inp DIN
.model DIN D(IS=1e-15 N={VCLMP/(VTN*log(1e-3/1e-15))} RS={RCLMP})

* ---- noise sources -------------------------------------------------------------
Rnv  nnv 0 1e3
Rnv2 nnv 0 1e15   ; PSpice: second connection at nnv
Ewn nwn 0 VALUE={(GENV)*V(nnv)}
Rnp  nnp 0 1e3
Rnp2 nnp 0 1e15   ; PSpice: second connection at nnp
Rnn  nnn 0 1e3
Rnn2 nnn 0 1e15   ; PSpice: second connection at nnn
Gnp 0 inp VALUE={(GNI)*V(nnp)}
Gnn 0 inn VALUE={(GNI)*V(nnn)}
Ifa  0 nfa DC {IFL}
Dfa  nfa 0 DFLK
Ifb  0 nfb DC {IFL}
Dfb  nfb 0 DQ
Efl  nfl 0 nfa nfb 1
.model DFLK D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFV} AF=1)
.model DQ   D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
* 1/f current noise, independent on each input (FCIN > 0)
Ifp1 0 nfp1 DC {IFL}
Dfp1 nfp1 0 DFLKI
Ifp2 0 nfp2 DC {IFL}
Dfp2 nfp2 0 DQ
Gfp 0 inp VALUE={(GFI)*V(nfp1,nfp2)}
Ifn1 0 nfn1 DC {IFL}
Dfn1 nfn1 0 DFLKI
Ifn2 0 nfn2 DC {IFL}
Dfn2 nfn2 0 DQ
Gfn 0 inn VALUE={(GFI)*V(nfn1,nfn2)}
.model DFLKI D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFI} AF=1)

* ---- CMRR and PSRR coupling into the DM input ----------------------------------
Ecm ncm0 0 VALUE={(0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))-VCMX}
.param FCMV={IF(FCMRR>0, FCMRR, 31.6*GBW/CMRR)}
Xcm  ncm0 ncm FDZCPL PARAMS: K={1/CMRR} FZ={FCMV}
Eps1 nps1i 0 VALUE={V(vcc)-VCCN}
.param FPSV={IF(FPSRR>0, FPSRR, 1e-3*GBW)}
.param FPSPV={IF(FPSRRP>0, FPSRRP, FPSV)}
.param FPSNV={IF(FPSRRN>0, FPSRRN, FPSV)}
Xps1 nps1i nps1 FDZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRP} FZ={FPSPV}
Eps2 nps2i 0 VALUE={V(vee)-VEEN}
Xps2 nps2i nps2 FDZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRN} FZ={FPSNV}

Evd vd 0 VALUE={V(inp)-V(inn)+VOS+V(ncm)+V(nps1)+V(nps2)+V(nwn)+V(nfl)+DVOST*(0.5*(1+tanh(((0.5
+ *(V(inp)+V(inn)))-V(vcc)+VCMT)/VKT)))}
* input common-mode range window: the top edge uses the lower input, the bottom
* edge the higher one (smooth min/max), so the stage works while one input is in
* range; times 1 - J for each conducting reversal junction (see below)
.param EPH={IF(PRHI>0, 1, 0)}
.param EPL={IF(PRLO>0, 1, 0)}
.param KJ={0.5/VTN}            ; 1/(2*VT): logistic of thermal width
* Input current: the same junction step, shifted by VT*ln(9) so that it is
* 0.9*IPR where the output flips (J = 1/2) and IPR beyond.
.param IPRV={IF(IPR>0, IPR, IMAXV)}
.param DJ={VTN*log(9)}
* junction functions of the reversal (0 when unused)
* (the two edge factors stay in one source: as separate nodes they made a
* transient with a 1 GH / 1 GF DC servo fail in tests/opamp_full_tests.cir)
Ewin nwin 0 VALUE={max(0.25*(1+tanh(((0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))+(0.5*sqrt((V(inp)-V(inn))*(V(inp)
+ -V(inn))+1e-4))-V(vee)-ICMLO)/VK))*(1+tanh((V(vcc)-ICMHI-(0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))+(0.5*sqrt((V(inp)
+ -V(inn))*(V(inp)-V(inn))+1e-4)))/VK)),1e-6) *(1-(EPH*0.5*(1+tanh((V(inp)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ))))*(1
+ -(EPH*0.5*(1+tanh((V(inn)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ))))*(1-(EPL*0.5*(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inp))*KJ))))
+ *(1-(EPL*0.5*(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inn))*KJ))))}

* ---- phase reversal through an input junction (PRHI, PRLO) ---------------------
* In a bipolar or JFET input pair a junction of the input device becomes forward
* biased when an input goes far enough beyond the range: the base-collector
* junction of an npn (at the top), the gate-drain junction of a p-JFET (at the
* bottom). Its current flows from the input pin straight into the high-impedance
* node of the first stage, in the direction opposite to the normal signal, and
* the saturated device no longer works as an amplifier. J (0..1) is the
* conduction of each junction (nodes njhp, njhn, njlp, njln above, used by Bwin,
* Bprp, Bprn and Bpr): a logistic step of thermal width centred VPRHI
* below vcc (VPRLO above vee). At full conduction the input pin carries IPR
* (into the pin at the top, out of it at the bottom), the stage gm is switched
* off, and PRHI*IMAX (PRLO*IMAX) is injected into the gain node: the output runs
* to the wrong rail at about PRHI*SR, faster than the slew rate for PRHI > 1.
* The output flips at half conduction, where the input current is 0.9*IPR, so
* a source resistance RS prevents the reversal while 0.9*RS*IPR exceeds the
* overdrive. IPR is about the tail current of the input pair (0 = SR*1pF).
* pin current: the junction logistic shifted by DJ = VT*ln(9), i.e. 9J/(1+8J)
Gprp inp 0 VALUE={IPRV*(9*(EPH*0.5*(1+tanh((V(inp)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ)))/(1+8*(EPH*0.5*(1
+ +tanh((V(inp)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ))))-9*(EPL*0.5*(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inp))*KJ)))/(1+8*(EPL*0.5
+ *(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inp))*KJ)))))}
Gprn inn 0 VALUE={IPRV*(9*(EPH*0.5*(1+tanh((V(inn)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ)))/(1+8*(EPH*0.5*(1
+ +tanh((V(inn)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ))))-9*(EPL*0.5*(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inn))*KJ)))/(1+8*(EPL*0.5
+ *(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inn))*KJ)))))}
* Injected current: IMAX*PR*J^(1+L), L = max(log2(PR),0). For PR >= 1 it
* equals the collapsing stage current IMAX*(1-J) at J = 1/2 whatever PR is, so
* the output flips at J = 1/2; at full conduction it is PR*IMAX.
.param LPH={max(log(max(PRHI,1e-3))/log(2),0)}
.param LPL={max(log(max(PRLO,1e-3))/log(2),0)}
.param AH={IMAXV*PRHI}
.param AL={IMAXV*PRLO}
Gpr 0 n1 VALUE={AH*(pwr((EPH*0.5*(1+tanh((V(inn)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ))),(1+LPH))-pwr((EPH*0.5*(1
+ +tanh((V(inp)-V(vcc)+VPRHI)*KJ))),(1+LPH)))+AL*(pwr((EPL*0.5*(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inp))*KJ)))
+ ,(1+LPL))-pwr((EPL*0.5*(1+tanh((V(vee)+VPRLO-V(inn))*KJ))),(1+LPL)))}

* ---- input-pair tail capacitance (KJUMP) ----------------------------------------
* The tail (common) node of the input pair follows the higher (KJUMP > 0,
* npn/nmos) or lower (KJUMP < 0, pnp/pmos) input (Solomon, IEEE JSSC 1974).
* TPL = sign(KJUMP). When a fast input step drives the tail, its charging
* current u = TPL*I(Vtl) > 0 is
* steered to the gain node, so the output of a follower jumps by |KJUMP| times
* the input step (in the uA741 the charge reaches the joined bases of the
* lateral pnps through an emitter-base junction, with current gain). On the
* other edge the tail follows the output slowly; its discharge current is
* small and is not modelled (u < 0 is ignored). Only input common-mode motion
* matters: a resistive inverter shows a smaller effect (its summing node moves
* while the output slews); small-signal analyses are unaffected.
.param TPL={IF(KJUMP<0, -1, 1)}
.param KTC={max(abs(KJUMP),1e-12)}
Etl ntl0 0 VALUE={(0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))+(0.5*TPL)*sqrt((V(inp)-V(inn))*(V(inp)-V(inn))+2.5e-3)}
* Ctl has a noiseless series resistance (time constant 1/(2*pi*FP3V)): the
* sensed current is then a smooth state, not the step-to-step ringing that
* trapezoidal integration gives in a capacitor driven by an ideal source
* (the max() below would rectify that ringing).
.param FP2V={IF(FP2>0, FP2, 3*GBW)}
.param FP3V={IF(FP3>0, FP3, 10*GBW)}
.param RTL={1/(PI2*FP3V*KTC*C1V)}
Vtl  ntl0 ntl 0
Gtl ntl ntlc VALUE={(1/RTL)*V(ntl,ntlc)}
Ctl  ntlc 0 {KTC*C1V}
Rtllk ntlc 0 1e15

* ---- DM gain node: n1 = differential output voltage ---------------------------
Ggm 0 n1 VALUE={tanh(GM0*V(vd)/IMAXV)*(IMAXV*V(nwin)+max(TPL*I(Vtl),0))}
G1 n1 0 VALUE={(1/R1V)*V(n1)}
C1   n1 0 {C1V}
R1lk n1 0 1e15
* symmetric differential swing limit set by the headroom around Vocm
Edlim ndl 0 VALUE={max(2*min(V(vcc)-VHD-V(vocm), V(vocm)-V(vee)-VLD), 10m)}
Eex0 nex0 0 VALUE={V(n1)-V(ndl)}
Eex1 nex1 0 VALUE={V(n1)+V(ndl)}
Gclp n1 0 VALUE={(IMAXV/1e-3)*(max(V(nex0),0)+min(V(nex1),0))}
G2   0 n2 n1 0 1m
G2r  n2 0 n2 0 1m
C2   n2 0 {1/(PI2*FP2V*1e3)}
R2lk n2 0 1e15
G3   0 n3 n2 0 1m
G3r  n3 0 n3 0 1m
C3   n3 0 {1/(PI2*FP3V*1e3)}
R3lk n3 0 1e15

* ---- Vocm pin: noiseless divider to mid-supply ------------------------------------
Gvo1 vcc vocm VALUE={(1/(2*RVOCM))*V(vcc,vocm)}
Gvo2 vocm vee VALUE={(1/(2*RVOCM))*V(vocm,vee)}
Cvo  vocm 0 {CVOCM}

* ---- CM loop: error amplifier (integrator + pole) -----------------------------
Eocs nocs 0 VALUE={0.5*(V(outp)+V(outn))-KBAL*(V(outp)-V(outn))}
Ggmc 0 nc1 VALUE={ICMV*tanh(GMC*(V(vocm)+VOSCM-V(nocs))/ICMV)}
Gc1 nc1 0 VALUE={(1/RCV)*V(nc1)}
Cc1  nc1 0 {C1V}
Rc1lk nc1 0 1e15
Echi nchi 0 VALUE={V(vcc)-VHD}
Eclo nclo 0 VALUE={V(vee)+VLD}
Eex2 nex2 0 VALUE={V(nc1)-V(nchi)}
Eex3 nex3 0 VALUE={V(nc1)-V(nclo)}
Gcclp nc1 0 VALUE={(ICMV/1e-3)*(max(V(nex2),0)+min(V(nex3),0))}
Gc2  0 cmo nc1 0 1m
Gc2r cmo 0 cmo 0 1m
.param FPCM2V={IF(FPCM2>0, FPCM2, 4*GBWCM)}
Cc2  cmo 0 {1/(PI2*FPCM2V*1e3)}
Rc2lk cmo 0 1e15

* ---- output stages ----------------------------------------------------------------
Edp ndp 0 VALUE={V(cmi)+0.5*V(n3)}
Edn ndn 0 VALUE={V(cmi)-0.5*V(n3)}
Evxp nvxp 0 VALUE={1e3*(V(ndp)-V(outp))}   ; vx in mV
Eicp nicp 0 VALUE={1e3*min(ISRC,max(-ISNK,((1e-3*V(nvxp))-0.5*VXO*tanh((1e-3*V(nvxp))/(VXO 
+ +1e-9)))/ROUT))}
Evxn nvxn 0 VALUE={1e3*(V(ndn)-V(outn))}   ; vx in mV
Eicn nicn 0 VALUE={1e3*min(ISRC,max(-ISNK,((1e-3*V(nvxn))-0.5*VXO*tanh((1e-3*V(nvxn))/(VXO 
+ +1e-9)))/ROUT))}
Gsrp vcc outp VALUE={0.5e-3*(V(nicp)+sqrt(V(nicp)*V(nicp)+1e-6))}
Gskp outp vee VALUE={0.5e-3*(sqrt(V(nicp)*V(nicp)+1e-6)-V(nicp))}
Gsrn vcc outn VALUE={0.5e-3*(V(nicn)+sqrt(V(nicn)*V(nicn)+1e-6))}
Gskn outn vee VALUE={0.5e-3*(sqrt(V(nicn)*V(nicn)+1e-6)-V(nicn))}
Iq   vcc vee DC {ICCQ}
Coutp outp 0 {COUT}
Coutn outn 0 {COUT}
* 100 Mohm noiseless leakage on each output: keeps the transient time step
* well-behaved when an output has no resistive load at all
Glkp outp 0 outp 0 1e-8
Glkn outn 0 outn 0 1e-8
.ends FDOPAMP_CORE

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* FDOPAMP_FULL: the normal model (CM loop closed internally).
* Pass parameters as usual, e.g.  X1 ... FDOPAMP_FULL PARAMS: GBW=200Meg
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt FDOPAMP_FULL inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm
+ PARAMS:
+ A0=100k GBW=100Meg SR=200Meg FP2=0 FP3=0
+ VOS=1m IB=2u IOS=0.1u
+ RID=1Meg CID=1p RIC=200Meg CIC=1p
+ CMRR=31.6k FCMRR=0 PSRRP=10k PSRRN=10k FPSRR=0 FPSRRP=0 FPSRRN=0 VCCN=5 VEEN=-5
+ VCMN=1e30
+ ENOISE=5n FCEN=1k INOISE=1p FCIN=0
+ ICCQ=10m VHD=1.2 VLD=1.2 ICMHI=1.5 ICMLO=1 VK=0.1
+ ROUT=10 ISRC=50m ISNK=50m VXO=0 COUT=1p
+ VCLMP=100 RCLMP=100 KJUMP=0
+ PRHI=0 PRLO=0 VPRHI=0 VPRLO=0 IPR=0 VCMT=1 VKT=0.1 DVOST=0 DIBT=0 KBAL=0
+ A0CM=10k GBWCM=50Meg FPCM2=0 SRCM=100Meg VOSCM=1m
+ RVOCM=50k CVOCM=1p
Xc inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm ncm ncm FDOPAMP_CORE PARAMS:
+ A0={A0} GBW={GBW} SR={SR} FP2={FP2} FP3={FP3}
+ VOS={VOS} IB={IB} IOS={IOS}
+ RID={RID} CID={CID} RIC={RIC} CIC={CIC}
+ CMRR={CMRR} FCMRR={FCMRR} PSRRP={PSRRP} PSRRN={PSRRN} FPSRR={FPSRR} FPSRRP={FPSRRP} FPSRRN={FPSRRN} VCCN={VCCN} VEEN={VEEN}
+ VCMN={VCMN}
+ ENOISE={ENOISE} FCEN={FCEN} INOISE={INOISE} FCIN={FCIN}
+ ICCQ={ICCQ} VHD={VHD} VLD={VLD} ICMHI={ICMHI} ICMLO={ICMLO} VK={VK}
+ ROUT={ROUT} ISRC={ISRC} ISNK={ISNK} VXO={VXO} COUT={COUT}
+ VCLMP={VCLMP} RCLMP={RCLMP} KJUMP={KJUMP}
+ PRHI={PRHI} PRLO={PRLO} VPRHI={VPRHI} VPRLO={VPRLO} IPR={IPR} VCMT={VCMT} VKT={VKT} DVOST={DVOST} DIBT={DIBT} KBAL={KBAL}
+ A0CM={A0CM} GBWCM={GBWCM} FPCM2={FPCM2} SRCM={SRCM} VOSCM={VOSCM}
+ RVOCM={RVOCM} CVOCM={CVOCM}
.ends FDOPAMP_FULL
